Z||000000||MR2KLR||11-29-2001||10:18 PM||||<BR>I just got the new Fuel pump instaled. But the car still won't run. The new pump turns on for 5 sec. when it turn on the key but the car will not start. t will start when I pour gass in the TBI unit. but then quickly die out. What's wrong now  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://members.tripod.com/wawoonigootphet/images/af/3in1_vu1.jpg">  <A HREF="http://community-2.webtv.net/TOMTOM81/MYNEWTOY/" TARGET=_blank>Tom's Page</A>||||reg||9
Z||000001||FieroMaster88||11-29-2001||10:28 PM||||The injector?  Plugged fuel filter?  2 things to look at!<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jamessig.jpg">                   <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>Not your ordinary 88 coupe!||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT-maniac||11-30-2001||01:52 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MR2KLR:<BR><B><BR>I just got the new Fuel pump instaled. But the car still won't run. The new pump turns on for 5 sec. when it turn on the key but the car will not start. t will start when I pour gass in the TBI unit. but then quickly die out. What's wrong now   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Try bypassing the oil pressure switch by hooking up a wire across the socket terminals. If the car starts that may be your problem. The oil pressure switch takes over control of the fuel pump after the first 5 seconds or so. It's an expensive item if you have to replace it.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||fiero56||11-30-2001||04:35 AM||||If the pump is priming with the engine off, the oil pressure switch will make no difference. Oil pressure switch is a safety. In case the fuel pump relay goes bad, the oil pressure switch will cover its a$$, and let you keep going.<P>Is the injector spitting fuel? If not, it could be mechanical, or electrical. Have you checked fuel pressure? Is the injector pulsing?||||reg||1
Z||000004||johnt671||11-30-2001||06:29 AM||||You may have a problem with the fuel pump relay or the ECM.  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||11-30-2001||06:39 AM||||loosen the fuel line at fuel rail and see if its pumping fuel up. make sure you do it with a COLD engine so you dont roast your car||||reg||1
Z||000006||MR2KLR||11-30-2001||03:46 PM||||I Put on a new fuel pump today, the old one was infact cloged. I cracked open a line on the EGR side of the TBI and fresh gas spewed out. I Then had my dad try to sart the car while I wached the injector behold no gas. I asume I have a bad injector the local parts store said $125  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"> for a new one  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> and the fiero store says $80 still not chump change.<P>Is there a way to check the circut to the Injector?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://members.tripod.com/wawoonigootphet/images/af/3in1_vu1.jpg">  <A HREF="http://community-2.webtv.net/TOMTOM81/MYNEWTOY/" TARGET=_blank>Tom's Page</A>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Rodrv6||11-30-2001||04:00 PM||||You can check the injector fairly easily.  Take the wire connector off and plug in an injector test light (noid light).  They are available at most parts stores.  Have someone crank the engine over and see if the light flashes.  If it does, then the injector is bad.  If it doesn't, then you either have a wiring problem or possibly an ECM problem.  One helpful hint-check the connections from the distributer to the wire harness carefully.  If the ECM doesn't "see" ignition pulse signals it won't fire the injector since it doesn't know the engine is turning.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  <BR>White 88 GT :)||||reg||1
